| 1 | Refactor: shared base class exagrype.api.CCZ4SolverBase; FOCCZ4Solver becomes a thin subclass (identical generated code) | done |
| 2 | exagrype.api.FOSOCCZ4Solver: 25 unknowns + auxiliary variables, hooks, initial condition wrapper, constraint enforcement of the evolved unknowns, lopsided advection quantities (all 25 evolved unknowns, as CCZ4SO=1 drops the advection from the kernels) | done |
| 3 | C++: exagrype::ccz4::reconstructFirstDerivativesFD4() | done |
| 4 | C++: split exagrype::ccz4::enforceCCZ4constraints() into evolved part + derivative part | done |
| 5 | exagrype.api.FOSOCCZ4Reconstructor for FD4 (task per RK stage) | done |
| 6 | Benchmark benchmarks/exagrype/fo_vs_so: FO vs SO with FD4 and lopsided advection | done, results below |
| 7 | Tests: Python (generated code, task graph; tests/unit/test_exagrype_fosoccz4_solver.py) and C++ (derivative reconstruction exact for cubics, constraint enforcement; ccz4/tests/FlatSpacetimeTest.cpp) | done |
| 8 | FV variants of the solver and the reconstructor | open |
